    "result_text": "Full suite is green. The full build shows `BUILD SUCCESS` with the acceptance test passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change enforces E.164 national-number length per country code in `OwnerTelephone.toE164` \u2014 the single place that produces the canonical telephone for both owner pipelines (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone` throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 400 when it returns empty).\n\nWhat I changed in `OwnerTelephone.java`:\n\n- Replaced the flat \"8\u201315 total digits\" check with a per-country rule. A small `NATIONAL_DIGITS` map declares the required national-number length for each recognised country code (`+61` \u2192 9, `+1` \u2192 10).\n- Added a `hasValidLength` helper that matches the longest known country-code prefix and requires the national number to be exactly that length; unrecognised country codes fall back to the generic E.164 8\u201315-digit range, preserving prior behaviour.\n\nSo `+61 123` (3 national digits) is now rejected specifically because 9 are required for `+61`, and the default-country path (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 national digits) still validates. Logic stays in the one telephone-normalization unit rather than being spread into the validation/normalize steps.",
